## Model card

- **Name:** GPT-5.1-Codex Mini
- **Short description:** OpenAI's smaller, more cost-effective, less-capable version of GPT-5.1-Codex (its own official one-line definition), aimed at high-volume agentic coding where cost matters more than peak capability. Variant/alias note: it is a distinct SKU in the GPT-5.1 Codex family, not a renamed GPT-5-Codex or a tier of Codex-Max.
- **Provider / access:** OpenAI API, model ID `gpt-5.1-codex-mini` (Responses API only — Chat Completions not supported). Codex-family recommendation applies: OpenAI advises using Codex-family models only for agentic coding in Codex-like environments.
- **Release / knowledge:** shipped with the GPT-5.1 / Codex-Max wave (Nov 19, 2025 per the launch-cycle coverage); knowledge cutoff Sep 30, 2024 (official docs).
- **IDs:** `openai/gpt-5.1-codex-mini` (no Free ID exists on OpenCode Zen — proprietary OpenAI endpoint only).
- **Context window:** 400,000 total tokens; 128,000 max output (official model docs — same window as the Codex-Max flagship).
- **Modalities:** text + image input; text output; reasoning-token support; function calling; structured outputs; web_search tool; prompt caching; evals + stored_completions support. Audio/video: no.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-19):** $0.25 / $2 per 1M input / output tokens; cached input $0.025 per 1M (official docs) — 5× cheaper on input and 5× cheaper on output than GPT-5-Codex / GPT-5.1-Codex-Max ($1.25/$10).
- **Architecture:** proprietary; smaller distilled-class member of the GPT-5.1 Codex reasoning family; parameter count not published.

